# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for EnigmaDB.
#
# Empty on purpose. Every entry added here is a race TSan found that we decided not
# to fix so each one needs a comment saying WHY. An unexplained suppression is
# indistinguishable from a bug someone silenced.
#
# Format (one per line):
#   race:SomeFunctionName
#   race:path/to/file.cpp
#   deadlock:SomeMutexWrapper
#   called_from_lib:libsomething.so
#
# Before adding one, check it isn't actually:
#   - a genuine race (fix it)
#   - a benign-looking race that is still UB in C++ (fix it "it works on x86" is
#     not a memory model)
#   - missing annotation on a custom synchronisation primitive (annotate it with
#     ANNOTATE_HAPPENS_BEFORE / ANNOTATE_HAPPENS_AFTER instead of suppressing)
